            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>A wild hunt rarely includes more than one or two huntsmasters, whose primary role is to gather and organize information about the quarry. They're also expert combatants who engage foes that can repel arrows or spells, and strike killing blows against minor quarry unworthy of the monarch's glaive.</p><hr /><p>Although some believe the wild hunt is nothing more than legend, the riders of the hunt are very real, comprised of countless lithe, horned humanoids, along with their steeds and hunting hounds. The term \"wild hunt\" refers to these fey as a whole, as well as to individual groups who gather at a wild hunt monarch's call to pursue their chosen quarry. The less dangerous a quarry, the more likely a monarch will impose rules to make the hunt more entertaining.</p>",
            "publication": {
